The files of one telcoin-network release, v0.99.0-adiri, as a dry run of
telcoin-network's etc/release.sh wrote them (RELEASE_DRY_RUN=1, three
components: the node, the worker gateway and the node record API).
gateway_pin_test.sh runs tools/check-gateway-pin.sh on them.

  keys/rehearsal.asc     the public half of the key the dry run signed with:
                         a throwaway key made for the dry run, never a release
                         key. Only its file name is changed, because a key file
                         in lib/release-keys is named after a maintainer's login.
  release/v0.99.0-adiri/ the release's edge files:
    SHA256SUMS-edge              the edge manifest: the IMAGE_DIGEST file and
                                 the tarball of the worker gateway and of the
                                 node record API
    SHA256SUMS-edge.asc          its signature by the throwaway key
    IMAGE_DIGEST-worker-gateway  the worker-gateway image the release names
    IMAGE_DIGEST-node-record-api the node record API image
  node/SHA256SUMS        the node manifest of the same dry run
  node/SHA256SUMS.asc    its signature by the same key

The files the manifests list are left out (the tarballs, the node's
IMAGE_DIGEST and chain configs), except the two edge IMAGE_DIGEST files: the
tool reads only the manifest lines and IMAGE_DIGEST-worker-gateway. The images
were pushed to the dry run's local registry, so both IMAGE_DIGEST files name
127.0.0.1:<port>/<name>, never ghcr.io.

Every file is as the dry run wrote it, byte for byte. Refresh them all together
from one new dry run: one directory under release/, named by a testnet or a
mainnet release tag. The test checks the release under the throwaway key only
with real gpg, and skips those checks once the key has expired; its other
checks copy these files and sign them with keys of their own.
